- Use a `std::unordered_map` to map keys to list iterators for O(1) lookup.
- `get(key)`: If key exists in map, move the corresponding node to the front of the list, return the value. Otherwise return a sentinel (e.g., `std::optional<Value>` in C++17).
- `put(key, value)`: If key exists, update value and move to front. If not, insert at front; if capacity exceeded, evict the least recently used (back of list).

